                <pb facs="0656" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v09/pg622"/>

                <head>238. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On December 6, President Eisenhower and his principal Cabinet officers briefed
                    President-elect Kennedy on the most significant world problems facing the United
                    States. In a review of the danger spots, Secretary Herter stated: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi>—This is acute and dangerous, and Mr.
                            Khrushchev has heavy pressure to get the Berlin question settled and to
                            stop the movement of refugees to the West from behind the Iron
                            Curtain.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>A memorandum for the record of this meeting is in the Eisenhower Library, Whitman
                    File, Presidential Transition Series.</p>
            </div>
